edits.newText:
/* ---- “Ausschnitte”: documented footprints of the filtered records ----
   The layer sits above the tiles/overlay and below the markers, the selected
   extent and the point crosshair. It is purely visual: pointer-events stay off
   so a map click keeps setting the point filter (the result list is the
   accessible way to select a record). Colours come from the cantonal palette
   (--zh-darkblue #00407c).

   Outline only, deliberately: the swisstopo series sheets all state the same
   Switzerland-wide extent, so per-record fills stacked into a solid blue slab.
   Identical extents are one rectangle (map.js) and only the hovered/selected
   footprint gets a fill. */
.map-footprint {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0 auto auto 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  border: 1px solid rgb(0 64 124 / 78%);
  pointer-events: none;
  will-change: transform;
}

/* A hovering/focused result row highlights the footprint it belongs to. */
.map-footprint.is-preview {
  border-width: 2px;
  border-color: var(--zh-darkblue);
  background: rgb(0 96 176 / 26%);
}

/* The selected record already has the strong dashed .map-extent on top; the
   footprint underneath just tells the same story with the rest of the set. */
.map-footprint.is-selected {
  border-style: dashed;
  border-color: var(--zh-black);
  background: rgb(0 64 124 / 14%);
}

